/-!
# Spectral flow of a path of self-adjoint Fredholm operators

The spectral flow of a continuous path `s ↦ A s` of bounded self-adjoint Fredholm operators on a
Hilbert space counts, with multiplicity, the eigenvalues of `A s` that cross `0` as `s` runs over
`[a, b]`, those crossing upwards positively. This file constructs it following Phillips.

A real number `c` is a **spectral-flow level** of a self-adjoint operator `T`
(`ContinuousLinearMap.IsSpectralFlowLevel`) if `c > 0`, neither `-c` nor `c` lies in the spectrum
of `T`, and the spectral projection of `T` for `[-c, c]` has finite rank. If `c` is a level of
every `A s` for `s ∈ [a, b]`, no eigenvalue of `A s` crosses `±c`, so the eigenvalues crossing `0`
are accounted for by the change of the rank of the spectral projection for `[0, c)`:

`finrank (range χ_[0, c) (A b)) - finrank (range χ_[0, c) (A a))`.

Along a general path a single level need not exist, but every self-adjoint Fredholm operator has a
level valid near it
(`IsSelfAdjoint.exists_pos_eventually_finrank_range_cfc_indicator_Icc_eq_of_isFredholm`), so
`[a, b]` can be cut into pieces each carrying one level. The relation
`TauCeti.HasSpectralFlow A a b n` records the values computed this way: it is generated by the
single-level formula on a piece and by concatenation. The value does not depend on the choices.

* **Independence of the level.** If `c` and `c'` are both levels along `[a, b]`, with `c' < c`,
  the two counts differ by the rank of the spectral projection for `[c', c)`, which is constant
  along `[a, b]` because neither `c'` nor `c` meets the spectrum. So both levels give the same
  value (`TauCeti.HasSpectralFlow.eq_of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel`).
* **Independence of the partition.** Every derivation of `HasSpectralFlow` can be split at any
  intermediate point (`TauCeti.HasSpectralFlow.exists_split`), and two derivations are compared
  piece by piece (`TauCeti.HasSpectralFlow.unique`).
* **Existence.** On a compact interval a value exists (`TauCeti.exists_hasSpectralFlow`), since the
  points joined to a given one by a derivation form an open and closed subset of `[a, b]`.

The spectral flow `TauCeti.spectralFlow A a b` is the value of any derivation, and `0` if there is
none. It is additive under concatenation of paths (`TauCeti.spectralFlow_add`), changes sign when
the path is reversed (`TauCeti.spectralFlow_comp_neg`) and vanishes along a path of invertible
operators (`TauCeti.spectralFlow_eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit`). For a path of real multiples
`f s • 1` of the identity of a finite-dimensional space the eigenvalue `f s` crosses `0` with the
multiplicity of the whole space (`TauCeti.spectralFlow_algebraMap`); for instance `f = tanh` on
`[-1, 1]` has spectral flow `dim H`.

## Main definitions

* `ContinuousLinearMap.IsSpectralFlowLevel T c`: `c` is a spectral-flow level of `T`.
* `TauCeti.HasSpectralFlow A a b n`: the path `A` has spectral flow `n` on `[a, b]`.
* `TauCeti.spectralFlow A a b`: the spectral flow of `A` on `[a, b]`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.HasSpectralFlow.unique`: the spectral flow is well defined.
* `TauCeti.exists_hasSpectralFlow`: a continuous path of self-adjoint Fredholm operators has a
  spectral flow on every compact interval.
* `TauCeti.spectralFlow_eq_of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel`: the spectral flow along a path with a
  single level.
* `TauCeti.spectralFlow_add`, `TauCeti.spectralFlow_comp_neg`: concatenation and reversal.
* `TauCeti.spectralFlow_const`, `TauCeti.spectralFlow_eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit`: the spectral flow
  vanishes along a constant path and along a path of invertible operators.
* `TauCeti.spectralFlow_algebraMap`: the spectral flow of a path of multiples of the identity.

## References

* J. Phillips, *Self-adjoint Fredholm operators and spectral flow*, Canad. Math. Bull. **39**
  (1996), 460--467.
* B. Booss-Bavnbek, M. Lesch and J. Phillips, *Unbounded Fredholm operators and spectral flow*,
  Canad. J. Math. **57** (2005), 225--250, Section 2.
-/

public section

open Filter Set Topology Module

variable {𝕜 H : Type*} [RCLike 𝕜] [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace 𝕜 H] [CompleteSpace H]
  [NormedAlgebra ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H)] [IsometricContinuousFunctionalCalculus ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H) IsSelfAdjoint]

namespace ContinuousLinearMap

/-- A **spectral-flow level** of an operator `T`: a number `c > 0` such that neither `-c` nor `c`
lies in the spectrum of `T` and the spectral projection of `T` for `[-c, c]` has finite rank. -/
structure IsSpectralFlowLevel (T : H →L[𝕜] H) (c : ℝ) : Prop where
  pos : 0 < c
  neg_notMem_spectrum : -c ∉ spectrum ℝ T
  notMem_spectrum : c ∉ spectrum ℝ T
  finiteDimensional_range :
    FiniteDimensional 𝕜 (cfc ((Icc (-c) c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) T).range

end ContinuousLinearMap

namespace TauCeti

open ContinuousLinearMap

/-- The path `A` of operators **has spectral flow `n` on `[a, b]`**. This relation is generated by
two rules. If a single `c` is a spectral-flow level of `A s` for every `s ∈ [a, b]`, the spectral
flow is the change of the rank of the spectral projection for `[0, c)` from `A a` to `A b`; and
spectral flows on adjacent intervals add. For a continuous path of self-adjoint operators with
closed range it relates each interval to at most one value (`TauCeti.HasSpectralFlow.unique`). -/
inductive HasSpectralFlow (A : ℝ → H →L[𝕜] H) : ℝ → ℝ → ℤ → Prop
  | of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel {a b c : ℝ} (hab : a ≤ b)
      (hc : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsSpectralFlowLevel c) :
      HasSpectralFlow A a b
        ((finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A b)).range : ℤ) -
          finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A a)).range)
  | trans {a b d : ℝ} {m n : ℤ} :
      HasSpectralFlow A a b m → HasSpectralFlow A b d n → HasSpectralFlow A a d (m + n)

variable {A : ℝ → H →L[𝕜] H} {a b d : ℝ} {m n : ℤ}

namespace HasSpectralFlow

/-- A spectral flow is only recorded on a nonempty interval. -/
theorem le (h : HasSpectralFlow A a b n) : a ≤ b := by
  induction h with
  | of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel hab => exact hab
  | trans _ _ h₁ h₂ => exact h₁.trans h₂

/-- **Splitting a spectral flow.** A derivation of the spectral flow on `[a, b]` splits at every
intermediate point into derivations on the two halves, with values adding up. -/
theorem exists_split (h : HasSpectralFlow A a b n) {s : ℝ} (hs : s ∈ Icc a b) :
    ∃ m k, HasSpectralFlow A a s m ∧ HasSpectralFlow A s b k ∧ m + k = n := by
  induction h generalizing s with
  | of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel _ hc =>
    refine ⟨_, _, of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel hs.1 fun t ht ↦ hc t ⟨ht.1, ht.2.trans hs.2⟩,
      of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel hs.2 fun t ht ↦ hc t ⟨hs.1.trans ht.1, ht.2⟩, ?_⟩
    ring
  | @trans a t d m₁ n₁ h₁ h₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
    rcases le_total s t with hst | hts
    · obtain ⟨m, k, hm, hk, rfl⟩ := ih₁ ⟨hs.1, hst⟩
      exact ⟨m, k + n₁, hm, hk.trans h₂, by ring⟩
    · obtain ⟨m, k, hm, hk, rfl⟩ := ih₂ ⟨hts, hs.2⟩
      exact ⟨m₁ + m, k, h₁.trans hm, hk, by ring⟩

/-- A derivation of the spectral flow on `[a, b]` restricts to every subinterval. -/
theorem exists_of_le (h : HasSpectralFlow A a b n) {s t : ℝ} (has : a ≤ s) (hst : s ≤ t)
    (htb : t ≤ b) : ∃ k, HasSpectralFlow A s t k := by
  obtain ⟨-, k, -, hk, -⟩ := h.exists_split ⟨has, hst.trans htb⟩
  obtain ⟨m, -, hm, -⟩ := hk.exists_split ⟨hst, htb⟩
  exact ⟨m, hm⟩

/-- Derivations of the spectral flow on two overlapping intervals give one on their union. -/
private theorem exists_min_max {p q r s : ℝ} (h₁ : HasSpectralFlow A p q m)
    (h₂ : HasSpectralFlow A r s n) (hrq : r ≤ q) (hps : p ≤ s) :
    ∃ k, HasSpectralFlow A (min p r) (max q s) k := by
  wlog hpr : p ≤ r generalizing p q r s m n
  · obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := this h₂ h₁ hps hrq (le_of_not_ge hpr)
    exact ⟨k, by rwa [min_comm, max_comm]⟩
  rw [min_eq_left hpr]
  rcases le_total s q with hsq | hqs
  · exact ⟨m, by rwa [max_eq_left hsq]⟩
  · obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h₂.exists_of_le hrq hqs le_rfl
    exact ⟨m + k, by rw [max_eq_right hqs]; exact h₁.trans hk⟩

end HasSpectralFlow

/-! ### Independence of the level -/

section Level

variable [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 (H →L[𝕜] H)]

/-- At an operator with closed range, the rank of the spectral projection for `[0, c)` adds over
the splitting `[0, c) = [0, c') ∪ [c', c)` at a smaller level `c'`. -/
private theorem finrank_range_cfc_indicator_Ico_eq {T : H →L[𝕜] H} (hT : IsSelfAdjoint T)
    (hR : IsClosed (T.range : Set H)) {c c' : ℝ} (hc : T.IsSpectralFlowLevel c)
    (hc' : T.IsSpectralFlowLevel c') (hcc' : c' < c) :
    (finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) T).range : ℤ) =
      finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c').indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) T).range +
        finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico c' c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) T).range := by
  -- The indicators involved are continuous on the spectrum: their frontiers meet it at most in
  -- `0`, which is isolated in the spectrum by the spectral gap.
  have hcont : ∀ {u v : ℝ}, u < v → (u = 0 ∨ u ∉ spectrum ℝ T) → v ∉ spectrum ℝ T →
      ContinuousOn ((Ico u v).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (spectrum ℝ T) := by
    intro u v huv hu hv
    refine hT.continuousOn_indicator_spectrum_of_isClosed_range hR fun x ⟨hx, hxs⟩ ↦ ?_
    rw [frontier_Ico huv] at hx
    rcases hx with rfl | rfl
    · exact hu.resolve_right (not_not_intro hxs)
    · exact absurd hxs hv
  have hcont' : ContinuousOn ((Icc (-c) c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (spectrum ℝ T) :=
    continuousOn_const.continuousOn_indicator_of_disjoint_frontier <| by
      rw [frontier_Icc (by linarith [hc.pos]), Set.disjoint_left]
      rintro x (rfl | rfl) hx
      exacts [hc.neg_notMem_spectrum hx, hc.notMem_spectrum hx]
  have h₁ := hcont hc'.pos (Or.inl rfl) hc'.notMem_spectrum
  have h₂ := hcont hcc' (Or.inr hc'.notMem_spectrum) hc.notMem_spectrum
  -- Both projections are dominated by the finite-rank projection for `[-c, c]`.
  have := hc.finiteDimensional_range
  have hfin : ∀ {Ω : Set ℝ}, Ω ⊆ Icc (-c) c →
      ContinuousOn (Ω.indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (spectrum ℝ T) →
      FiniteDimensional 𝕜 (cfc (Ω.indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) T).range := fun hΩ hΩc ↦
    Submodule.finiteDimensional_of_le (range_cfc_indicator_mono hΩ hΩc hcont')
  have := hfin (Ω := Ico 0 c') (fun x hx ↦ ⟨by linarith [hx.1, hc.pos], hx.2.le.trans hcc'.le⟩) h₁
  have := hfin (Ω := Ico c' c) (fun x hx ↦ ⟨by linarith [hx.1, hc'.pos], hx.2.le⟩) h₂
  rw [← Ico_union_Ico_eq_Ico hc'.pos.le hcc'.le,
    finrank_range_cfc_indicator_union Ico_disjoint_Ico_same h₁ h₂, Nat.cast_add]

/-- **Independence of the level.** Along a continuous path of self-adjoint operators with closed
range, two spectral-flow levels valid on all of `[a, b]` give the same count. -/
private theorem sub_eq_sub_of_isSpectralFlowLevel (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b))
    (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s))
    (hR : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsClosed ((A s).range : Set H)) (hab : a ≤ b) {c c' : ℝ}
    (hc : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsSpectralFlowLevel c)
    (hc' : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsSpectralFlowLevel c') :
    (finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A b)).range : ℤ) -
        finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A a)).range =
      (finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c').indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A b)).range : ℤ) -
        finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c').indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A a)).range := by
  wlog hcc' : c' < c generalizing c c'
  · rcases (not_lt.1 hcc').lt_or_eq with h | rfl
    · exact (this hc' hc h).symm
    · rfl
  have ha : a ∈ Icc a b := ⟨le_rfl, hab⟩
  have hb : b ∈ Icc a b := ⟨hab, le_rfl⟩
  have hda := finrank_range_cfc_indicator_Ico_eq (hsa a ha) (hR a ha) (hc a ha) (hc' a ha) hcc'
  have hdb := finrank_range_cfc_indicator_Ico_eq (hsa b hb) (hR b hb) (hc b hb) (hc' b hb) hcc'
  -- The rank for `[c', c)` is constant along the path.
  have hrank := isPreconnected_Icc.rank_range_cfc_indicator_eq hA hsa (Ω := Ico c' c)
    (fun s hs ↦ by
      rw [frontier_Ico hcc', Set.disjoint_left]
      rintro x (rfl | rfl) hx
      exacts [(hc' s hs).notMem_spectrum hx, (hc s hs).notMem_spectrum hx]) ha hb
  have : finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico c' c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A a)).range =
      finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico c' c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A b)).range :=
    congr_arg Cardinal.toNat hrank
  rw [hda, hdb, this]
  ring

namespace HasSpectralFlow

/-- **The single-level formula.** If `c` is a spectral-flow level of `A s` for every `s ∈ [a, b]`,
every value of the spectral flow on `[a, b]` is the change of the rank of the spectral projection
for `[0, c)`. -/
theorem eq_of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel (h : HasSpectralFlow A a b n)
    (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b)) (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s))
    (hR : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsClosed ((A s).range : Set H)) {c : ℝ}
    (hc : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsSpectralFlowLevel c) :
    n = (finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A b)).range : ℤ) -
      finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A a)).range := by
  induction h with
  | of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel hab hc' =>
    exact sub_eq_sub_of_isSpectralFlowLevel hA hsa hR hab hc' hc
  | @trans a t d m n h₁ h₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
    have hat := h₁.le
    have htd := h₂.le
    have hsub₁ : Icc a t ⊆ Icc a d := Icc_subset_Icc le_rfl htd
    have hsub₂ : Icc t d ⊆ Icc a d := Icc_subset_Icc hat le_rfl
    rw [ih₁ (hA.mono hsub₁) (fun s hs ↦ hsa s (hsub₁ hs)) (fun s hs ↦ hR s (hsub₁ hs))
      (fun s hs ↦ hc s (hsub₁ hs)), ih₂ (hA.mono hsub₂) (fun s hs ↦ hsa s (hsub₂ hs))
      (fun s hs ↦ hR s (hsub₂ hs)) (fun s hs ↦ hc s (hsub₂ hs))]
    ring

/-- **The spectral flow is well defined.** Along a continuous path of self-adjoint operators with
closed range, any two derivations of the spectral flow on `[a, b]` have the same value. -/
theorem unique (hm : HasSpectralFlow A a b m) (hn : HasSpectralFlow A a b n)
    (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b)) (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s))
    (hR : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsClosed ((A s).range : Set H)) : m = n := by
  induction hm generalizing n with
  | of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel _ hc =>
    exact (hn.eq_of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel hA hsa hR hc).symm
  | @trans a t d m₁ n₁ h₁ h₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
    have hat := h₁.le
    have htd := h₂.le
    have hsub₁ : Icc a t ⊆ Icc a d := Icc_subset_Icc le_rfl htd
    have hsub₂ : Icc t d ⊆ Icc a d := Icc_subset_Icc hat le_rfl
    obtain ⟨m, k, hm, hk, rfl⟩ := hn.exists_split ⟨hat, htd⟩
    rw [ih₁ hm (hA.mono hsub₁) (fun s hs ↦ hsa s (hsub₁ hs)) (fun s hs ↦ hR s (hsub₁ hs)),
      ih₂ hk (hA.mono hsub₂) (fun s hs ↦ hsa s (hsub₂ hs)) (fun s hs ↦ hR s (hsub₂ hs))]

omit [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 (H →L[𝕜] H)] in
/-- Along a path of invertible self-adjoint operators every spectral flow vanishes: no eigenvalue
crosses `0`. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit (h : HasSpectralFlow A a b n) (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b))
    (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s)) (hu : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsUnit (A s)) : n = 0 := by
  induction h with
  | @of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel a b c hab hc =>
    have hrank := isPreconnected_Icc.rank_range_cfc_indicator_eq hA hsa (Ω := Ico 0 c)
      (fun s hs ↦ by
        rw [frontier_Ico (hc s hs).pos, Set.disjoint_left]
        rintro x (rfl | rfl) hx
        exacts [spectrum.zero_notMem ℝ (hu s hs) hx, (hc s hs).notMem_spectrum hx])
      ⟨hab, le_rfl⟩ ⟨le_rfl, hab⟩
    have : finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A b)).range =
        finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A a)).range :=
      congr_arg Cardinal.toNat hrank
    rw [this, sub_self]
  | @trans a t d m n h₁ h₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
    have hsub₁ : Icc a t ⊆ Icc a d := Icc_subset_Icc le_rfl h₂.le
    have hsub₂ : Icc t d ⊆ Icc a d := Icc_subset_Icc h₁.le le_rfl
    rw [ih₁ (hA.mono hsub₁) (fun s hs ↦ hsa s (hsub₁ hs)) (fun s hs ↦ hu s (hsub₁ hs)),
      ih₂ (hA.mono hsub₂) (fun s hs ↦ hsa s (hsub₂ hs)) (fun s hs ↦ hu s (hsub₂ hs)), add_zero]

end HasSpectralFlow

end Level

/-! ### Reversal -/

/-- Reversing the path negates the spectral flow. -/
theorem HasSpectralFlow.comp_neg (h : HasSpectralFlow A a b n) :
    HasSpectralFlow (fun s ↦ A (-s)) (-b) (-a) (-n) := by
  induction h with
  | of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel hab hc =>
    have := HasSpectralFlow.of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel (A := fun s ↦ A (-s))
      (neg_le_neg hab) fun s hs ↦ hc (-s) ⟨le_neg.1 hs.2, neg_le.1 hs.1⟩
    convert this using 1
    rw [neg_neg, neg_neg]
    ring
  | trans _ _ ih₁ ih₂ =>
    convert ih₂.trans ih₁ using 1
    ring

variable [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 (H →L[𝕜] H)]

/-! ### Existence -/

section Existence

/-- Near every point of `[a, b]`, a continuous path of self-adjoint Fredholm operators has a
common spectral-flow level on a whole interval. -/
private theorem exists_isSpectralFlowLevel (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b))
    (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s)) (hF : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsFredholm) {x : ℝ}
    (hx : x ∈ Icc a b) :
    ∃ c, ∃ ε > 0, ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, dist s x < ε → (A s).IsSpectralFlowLevel c := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hev⟩ :=
    (hsa x hx).exists_pos_eventually_finrank_range_cfc_indicator_Icc_eq_of_isFredholm (hF x hx)
  have ht : Tendsto A (𝓝[Icc a b] x) (𝓝[{S | IsSelfAdjoint S}] (A x)) :=
    tendsto_nhdsWithin_iff.2 ⟨hA x hx, eventually_nhdsWithin_of_forall hsa⟩
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩ := Metric.mem_nhdsWithin_iff.1 (ht hev)
  exact ⟨c, ε, hε, fun s hs hsx ↦
    have h := hball ⟨Metric.mem_ball.2 hsx, hs⟩
    ⟨hc, h.1, h.2.1, h.2.2.1⟩⟩

/-- **Existence of the spectral flow.** A path of self-adjoint Fredholm operators which is
continuous on `[a, b]` has a spectral flow there. -/
theorem exists_hasSpectralFlow (hab : a ≤ b) (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b))
    (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s)) (hF : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsFredholm) :
    ∃ n, HasSpectralFlow A a b n := by
  -- Points joined by a derivation over the interval between them form a transitive relation
  -- which holds near every point, hence on all of `[a, b]`.
  let P : ℝ → ℝ → Prop := fun x y ↦ ∃ n, HasSpectralFlow A (min x y) (max x y) n
  suffices P a b by simpa [P, min_eq_left hab, max_eq_right hab] using this
  refine isPreconnected_Icc.induction₂ P (fun x hx ↦ ?_) (fun x y z _ _ _ hxy hyz ↦ ?_)
    (fun x y _ _ ⟨n, hn⟩ ↦ ⟨n, by rwa [min_comm, max_comm]⟩) ⟨le_rfl, hab⟩ ⟨hab, le_rfl⟩
  · obtain ⟨c, ε, hε, hc⟩ := exists_isSpectralFlowLevel hA hsa hF hx
    filter_upwards [inter_mem_nhdsWithin (Icc a b) (Metric.ball_mem_nhds x hε)] with y hy
    refine ⟨_, HasSpectralFlow.of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel min_le_max fun s hs ↦ hc s ?_ ?_⟩
    · exact ⟨le_trans (le_min hx.1 hy.1.1) hs.1, hs.2.trans (max_le hx.2 hy.1.2)⟩
    · rw [dist_comm]
      exact (Real.dist_left_le_of_mem_uIcc hs).trans_lt (by rw [dist_comm]; exact hy.2)
  · -- The two intervals both contain `y`, so their union is an interval containing `[x, z]`.
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hxy
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hyz
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hm.exists_min_max hn
      ((min_le_left y z).trans (le_max_right x y)) ((min_le_right x y).trans (le_max_left y z))
    exact hk.exists_of_le
      (le_min ((min_le_left _ _).trans (min_le_left _ _))
        ((min_le_right _ _).trans (min_le_right _ _))) min_le_max
      (max_le ((le_max_left _ _).trans (le_max_left _ _))
        ((le_max_right _ _).trans (le_max_right _ _)))

end Existence

/-! ### The spectral flow -/

open Classical in
/-- The **spectral flow** of a path `A` of operators on `[a, b]`: the value of any derivation of
`TauCeti.HasSpectralFlow A a b`, and `0` if there is none. For a continuous path of self-adjoint
Fredholm operators and `a ≤ b` a derivation exists (`TauCeti.exists_hasSpectralFlow`) and all
derivations have the same value (`TauCeti.HasSpectralFlow.unique`). This is Phillips' count, with
multiplicity, of the eigenvalues of `A s` crossing `0` as `s` runs from `a` to `b`, those crossing
upwards counted positively. -/
noncomputable def spectralFlow (A : ℝ → H →L[𝕜] H) (a b : ℝ) : ℤ :=
  if h : ∃ n, HasSpectralFlow A a b n then h.choose else 0

/-- The spectral flow is the value of every derivation. -/
theorem HasSpectralFlow.spectralFlow_eq (h : HasSpectralFlow A a b n)
    (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b)) (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s))
    (hR : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsClosed ((A s).range : Set H)) : spectralFlow A a b = n := by
  have hex : ∃ n, HasSpectralFlow A a b n := ⟨n, h⟩
  rw [spectralFlow, dite_eq_left_of_eq_true (eq_true hex)]
  exact hex.choose_spec.unique h hA hsa hR

/-- A continuous path of self-adjoint Fredholm operators has its spectral flow on `[a, b]`. -/
theorem hasSpectralFlow_spectralFlow (hab : a ≤ b) (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b))
    (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s)) (hF : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsFredholm) :
    HasSpectralFlow A a b (spectralFlow A a b) := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := exists_hasSpectralFlow hab hA hsa hF
  rwa [hn.spectralFlow_eq hA hsa fun s hs ↦ (hF s hs).isClosed_range]

/-- **The single-level formula for the spectral flow.** If a single `c` is a spectral-flow level of
`A s` for every `s ∈ [a, b]`, the spectral flow on `[a, b]` is the change of the rank of the
spectral projection for `[0, c)`. -/
theorem spectralFlow_eq_of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel (hab : a ≤ b)
    (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b)) (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s))
    (hR : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsClosed ((A s).range : Set H)) {c : ℝ}
    (hc : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsSpectralFlowLevel c) :
    spectralFlow A a b =
      (finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A b)).range : ℤ) -
        finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (A a)).range :=
  (HasSpectralFlow.of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel hab hc).spectralFlow_eq hA hsa hR

/-- **Concatenation.** The spectral flow on `[a, d]` is the sum of the spectral flows on `[a, b]`
and on `[b, d]`. -/
theorem spectralFlow_add (hab : a ≤ b) (hbd : b ≤ d) (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a d))
    (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a d, IsSelfAdjoint (A s)) (hF : ∀ s ∈ Icc a d, (A s).IsFredholm) :
    spectralFlow A a b + spectralFlow A b d = spectralFlow A a d := by
  have hsub₁ : Icc a b ⊆ Icc a d := Icc_subset_Icc le_rfl hbd
  have hsub₂ : Icc b d ⊆ Icc a d := Icc_subset_Icc hab le_rfl
  have h₁ := hasSpectralFlow_spectralFlow hab (hA.mono hsub₁) (fun s hs ↦ hsa s (hsub₁ hs))
    fun s hs ↦ hF s (hsub₁ hs)
  have h₂ := hasSpectralFlow_spectralFlow hbd (hA.mono hsub₂) (fun s hs ↦ hsa s (hsub₂ hs))
    fun s hs ↦ hF s (hsub₂ hs)
  exact ((h₁.trans h₂).spectralFlow_eq hA hsa fun s hs ↦ (hF s hs).isClosed_range).symm

/-- The spectral flow over a single point vanishes. -/
theorem spectralFlow_self (hsa : IsSelfAdjoint (A a)) (hF : (A a).IsFredholm) :
    spectralFlow A a a = 0 := by
  have hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a a) := by rw [Icc_self]; exact continuousOn_singleton _ _
  have hmem : ∀ s ∈ Icc a a, s = a := fun s hs ↦ le_antisymm hs.2 hs.1
  have hsa' : ∀ s ∈ Icc a a, IsSelfAdjoint (A s) := fun s hs ↦ hmem s hs ▸ hsa
  have hF' : ∀ s ∈ Icc a a, (A s).IsFredholm := fun s hs ↦ hmem s hs ▸ hF
  have h := hasSpectralFlow_spectralFlow le_rfl hA hsa' hF'
  have := (h.trans h).spectralFlow_eq hA hsa' fun s hs ↦ (hF' s hs).isClosed_range
  omega

/-- A constant path of self-adjoint Fredholm operators has spectral flow `0`. -/
theorem spectralFlow_const {T : H →L[𝕜] H} (hab : a ≤ b) (hT : IsSelfAdjoint T)
    (hF : T.IsFredholm) : spectralFlow (fun _ ↦ T) a b = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hev⟩ :=
    hT.exists_pos_eventually_finrank_range_cfc_indicator_Icc_eq_of_isFredholm hF
  obtain ⟨hneg, hpos, hfin, -⟩ := hev.self_of_nhdsWithin (show T ∈ {S | IsSelfAdjoint S} from hT)
  rw [spectralFlow_eq_of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel hab continuousOn_const (fun _ _ ↦ hT)
    (fun _ _ ↦ hF.isClosed_range) fun _ _ ↦ ⟨hc, hneg, hpos, hfin⟩, sub_self]

/-- **Reversal.** Running a path backwards negates its spectral flow. -/
theorem spectralFlow_comp_neg (hab : a ≤ b) (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b))
    (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s)) (hF : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsFredholm) :
    spectralFlow (fun s ↦ A (-s)) (-b) (-a) = -spectralFlow A a b := by
  have hmem : ∀ s ∈ Icc (-b) (-a), -s ∈ Icc a b := fun s hs ↦ ⟨le_neg.1 hs.2, neg_le.1 hs.1⟩
  refine (hasSpectralFlow_spectralFlow hab hA hsa hF).comp_neg.spectralFlow_eq ?_
    (fun s hs ↦ hsa _ (hmem s hs)) fun s hs ↦ (hF _ (hmem s hs)).isClosed_range
  exact hA.comp continuousOn_neg fun s hs ↦ hmem s hs

/-- Along a path of invertible self-adjoint operators the spectral flow vanishes. -/
theorem spectralFlow_eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit (hab : a ≤ b) (hA : ContinuousOn A (Icc a b))
    (hsa : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsSelfAdjoint (A s)) (hu : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, IsUnit (A s)) :
    spectralFlow A a b = 0 := by
  have hF : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (A s).IsFredholm := fun s hs ↦ by
    obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hu s hs
    exact he ▸ ContinuousLinearEquiv.isFredholm (ContinuousLinearEquiv.unitsEquiv 𝕜 H e)
  exact (hasSpectralFlow_spectralFlow hab hA hsa hF).eq_zero_of_forall_isUnit hA hsa hu

/-! ### Paths of multiples of the identity -/

section Scalar

omit [CompleteSpace H] [IsometricContinuousFunctionalCalculus ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H) IsSelfAdjoint]
  [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 (H →L[𝕜] H)] in
/-- The spectrum of a real multiple `r • 1` of the identity is contained in `{r}`. -/
private theorem eq_of_mem_spectrum_algebraMap {r x : ℝ}
    (hx : x ∈ spectrum ℝ (algebraMap ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H) r)) : x = r := by
  by_contra hxr
  refine hx ?_
  rw [spectrum.mem_resolventSet_iff, ← map_sub]
  exact (isUnit_iff_ne_zero.2 (sub_ne_zero.2 hxr)).map _

omit [IsometricContinuousFunctionalCalculus ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H) IsSelfAdjoint] in
/-- A real multiple of the identity is self-adjoint. -/
private theorem isSelfAdjoint_algebraMap (r : ℝ) :
    IsSelfAdjoint (algebraMap ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H) r) := by
  rw [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, ← algebraMap_smul 𝕜 r (1 : H →L[𝕜] H)]
  refine IsSelfAdjoint.smul ?_ (IsSelfAdjoint.one _)
  rw [RCLike.algebraMap_eq_ofReal]
  exact RCLike.conj_ofReal r

omit [IsScalarTower ℝ 𝕜 (H →L[𝕜] H)] in
/-- The number of eigenvalues of `r • 1` in `[0, c)`, for `|r| < c`: all of them if `0 ≤ r`, and
none otherwise. -/
private theorem finrank_range_cfc_indicator_Ico_algebraMap {r c : ℝ}
    (hrc : r < c) :
    (finrank 𝕜 (cfc ((Ico 0 c).indicator (1 : ℝ → ℝ)) (algebraMap ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H) r)).range : ℤ) =
      if 0 ≤ r then (finrank 𝕜 H : ℤ) else 0 := by
  rw [cfc_algebraMap]
  split_ifs with hr
  · rw [indicator_of_mem (show r ∈ Ico 0 c from ⟨hr, hrc⟩), Pi.one_apply, map_one,
      LinearMap.range_eq_top.2 fun x ↦ ⟨x, rfl⟩, finrank_top]
  · rw [indicator_of_notMem (show r ∉ Ico 0 c from fun h ↦ hr h.1), map_zero,
      ContinuousLinearMap.toLinearMap_zero, LinearMap.range_zero, finrank_bot, Nat.cast_zero]

/-- **A scalar crossing.** On a finite-dimensional space, along a path `s ↦ f s • 1` of real
multiples of the identity, the eigenvalue `f s` has multiplicity `dim H`, and the spectral flow is
`dim H` times the change of the indicator of `0 ≤ f s`. For instance it is `dim H` for `f = tanh`
on `[-1, 1]`, and `-dim H` for `f = -tanh`. -/
theorem spectralFlow_algebraMap [FiniteDimensional 𝕜 H] {f : ℝ → ℝ} (hab : a ≤ b)
    (hf : ContinuousOn f (Icc a b)) :
    spectralFlow (fun s ↦ algebraMap ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H) (f s)) a b =
      finrank 𝕜 H * ((if 0 ≤ f b then 1 else 0) - if 0 ≤ f a then 1 else 0) := by
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := isCompact_Icc.exists_bound_of_continuousOn hf
  set c := max C 0 + 1
  have hlt : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, |f s| < c := fun s hs ↦
    (Real.norm_eq_abs _ ▸ hC s hs).trans_lt ((le_max_left C 0).trans_lt (lt_add_one _))
  have hlevel : ∀ s ∈ Icc a b, (algebraMap ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H) (f s)).IsSpectralFlowLevel c :=
    fun s hs ↦
    { pos := by positivity
      neg_notMem_spectrum := fun h ↦ by
        have := eq_of_mem_spectrum_algebraMap h
        linarith [neg_abs_le (f s), hlt s hs]
      notMem_spectrum := fun h ↦ by
        have := eq_of_mem_spectrum_algebraMap h
        linarith [le_abs_self (f s), hlt s hs]
      finiteDimensional_range := inferInstance }
  have hcont : Continuous (algebraMap ℝ (H →L[𝕜] H)) :=
    AddMonoidHomClass.continuous_of_bound _ ‖(1 : H →L[𝕜] H)‖ fun r ↦ by
      rw [norm_algebraMap, mul_comm]
  rw [spectralFlow_eq_of_forall_isSpectralFlowLevel (A := fun s ↦ algebraMap ℝ _ (f s)) hab
    (hcont.comp_continuousOn hf)
    (fun s _ ↦ isSelfAdjoint_algebraMap (f s))
    (fun s _ ↦ Submodule.isClosed_of_finiteDimensional _) hlevel,
    finrank_range_cfc_indicator_Ico_algebraMap ((le_abs_self _).trans_lt (hlt b ⟨hab, le_rfl⟩)),
    finrank_range_cfc_indicator_Ico_algebraMap ((le_abs_self _).trans_lt (hlt a ⟨le_rfl, hab⟩))]
  split_ifs <;> ring

end Scalar

end TauCeti
